## Props

An `<input type="search">` with a visually hidden `<label>` and a clear button that shows while it holds text. Escape clears the text and keeps focus; on an empty field Escape goes on to the screen, so PageHeader's `backOnEscape` backs out. Clearing returns focus to the field.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `label` (required) | `string` |  | The field's name for assistive tech, such as "Filter hosts". It's a real `<label>`, visually hidden. |
| `value` | `string` |  | Controlled text. |
| `defaultValue` | `string` |  | Text at first, when uncontrolled. Default `''`. |
| `onValueChange` | `(value: string) => void` |  | Runs with the new text on every change: typing, the clear button and Escape. |
| `placeholder` | `string` |  | Text shown while the field is empty. Default the `label`. |
| `size` | `'md' \| 'lg'` |  |  |
| `className` | `string` |  | On the wrapper `<div>` that holds the label, the field and the clear button. |
| `ref` | `React.Ref<HTMLInputElement>` |  |  |

SearchField also takes the attributes of `<input>`, such as `aria-describedby`.

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import * as React from 'react';
import { ListGroup, ListRow } from '@/components/lede/list';
import { SearchField } from '@/components/lede/search-field';

export function HostList({ hosts }: { hosts: { id: string; name: string }[] }) {
  const [query, setQuery] = React.useState('');
  const shown = hosts.filter((h) => h.name.toLowerCase().includes(query.trim().toLowerCase()));
  return (
    <>
      <SearchField label="Filter hosts" value={query} onValueChange={setQuery} />
      <ListGroup title="Hosts" summary={query ? `${shown.length} of ${hosts.length}` : `${hosts.length}`}>
        {shown.map((h) => <ListRow key={h.id} title={h.name} href={`/hosts/${h.id}`} />)}
      </ListGroup>
    </>
  );
}
```

Docs: [Components](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/components.md).

